 "puzzleThemes": [],
 "intro": {
  "text": "The Sicilian Defence, 1...c5, is the most popular answer to 1.e4. You do not copy White in the centre: your c-pawn fights for the d4 square, and when White opens the game with d4, you trade that side pawn for White's centre pawn. You get an extra centre pawn and an open road for your rooks on the c-file, while White gets more space and quicker development. In the Dragon set-up taught here, your bishop goes to g7 and your king castles behind it."
 },
