     "notes": {
      "text": "1...c5 controls d4 from the side instead of meeting e4 head on. About half the time White answers with 2.Nf3, often followed by 3.d4 as in this Lesson. Against 2.Bc4, which aims at f7, play ...e6 to block the bishop's diagonal; against 2.c3, which gets ready for d4 with a pawn, attack e4 at once with 2...Nf6 or 2...d5; against 2.Nc3, use the same set-up as here, with ...g6, ...Bg7, ...d6 and ...Nc6."
     }
