      "text": "White opens the centre with 3.d4. 3...cxd4 takes, and this trade is the heart of the Sicilian. Your c-pawn is gone, but so is White's d-pawn, so you have two centre pawns (d6 and e7) against White's one (e4). The c-file is now half-open: none of your pawns stands on it, so your rooks can use it later."
